<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramon I of Pallars and Ribagorza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 920</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramon I was the first independent count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallars">Pallars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ribagorza">Ribagorza</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>. Around 872 he broke away from the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> and made the two mountain counties a hereditary lordship of his own. He fought Muslim neighbours and married into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a>. After his death his sons divided the counties, separating Pallars and Ribagorza.</p></div>
